{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head 77cbe18c940b28476a3399e62aa4abe8a32e3ffd under Hugh's request b33d61ec2005984b63615d081d4147b61950175c. Two repairs remain on the existing commitment.\n\n1. Preserve the live publication when an older command is retried. cmd/gs/artifact.go:113 combines a replayed artifact with newly planned retirements without proving that the replayed successor is still live. Reproduction: publish path return.txt at head A on promise P with an explicit --branch; publish its recut B on P; rerun the identical A publication. A's artifact key replays the already retired artifact, while the new retirement retires B and rests on that dead A pointer. The command succeeds, prints the retired A identifier as its reporting artifact and leaves zero live artifacts for the path. I reproduced this with the real workflow fixture and normal fold preflight; the existing preflight does not prevent it. This turns a retry into withdrawal of the current publication. Before any append, refuse a publication whose would-be successor resolves to a retired artifact (with a useful repair), or otherwise guarantee a genuinely live successor without reviving the old event. Add the A -\u003e B -\u003e retry A regression, proving B stays live and no retirement lands on refusal. Keep the ordinary interrupted-publication and same-head retry behavior. Evidence: /tmp/codex-recut-overlay_test.go, /tmp/codex-recut-overlay.json, /tmp/codex-recut-return-head.log. Run: go test -overlay /tmp/codex-recut-overlay.json ./cmd/gs -run '^TestCodexRepublishAnEarlierRetiredHead$' -count=1 -v.\n\n2. The mixed-head refusal still promises a repair that does not work for a cited artifact at a path republished at B. cmd/gs/review_request.go:223 says publishing again clears the set and limits the cited-pointer exception to a path the head no longer changes. keepUncited skips cited pointers at recurring paths too. The existing TestReviewRequestStillRefusesAMixedSetTheRepublishCouldNotClear already builds exactly this case, but tests only the presence of command substrings. Repeating gs artifact while cites.md still cites A leaves the same mixed set. Name the cited-pointer repair regardless of whether the path recurs: repoint to B where a successor exists, then retire the old pointer; distinguish the dropped-path no-successor case. Correct the matching review-request.md table row and pin the actual repair flow, not just that the error mentions both commands. This is required by the request's explicit outcome and condition 4.\n\nArchitecture: layer 7 CLI orchestration changes artifact publication into publication plus same-lane retirements. The architecture candidate records that contract, and all four documentation artifacts rest on the corresponding implementation artifacts. Kernel, fold authority, and merge succession rules remain unchanged. The contract is not yet satisfied because the old-head retry can remove the only live publication.\n\nSecurity: the selector correctly bounds automated retirement to the signer, direct named-promise provenance, another head, and live artifacts. Same-head, other-promise and other-actor protections pass. Change-set uncertainty and unnamed still-changed paths preserve pointers; citation lookup failures also preserve them. Local signing and normal admission remain intact. However the replayed-successor defect is an unresolved destructive-operation safety issue within the actor's own lane; disclosing the plan and fold preflight do not make a retired successor live. A wrong own --promise remains an intentional choice of lane, with the disclosed plan as the current warning, not an independent authorization check.\n\nSimplification: the shared lane selector and three-case retirement plan are appropriate. Fix successor liveness at this orchestration boundary and simplify the repair wording; no new lifecycle or duplicated fold mechanism is needed.\n\nValidation: independently ran the focused artifact retirement, mixed-head, partial publication, unmeasured target, basis refusal and preflight tests under -race (29.601s, pass). The additional retry regression fails as described. Inspected retained lane1-full-r2.log (36 packages, FULL_EXIT=0), lane1-cmdgs-r2.log and docset log; the checkout is clean at the exact head. This verdict names the reporting test artifact first and all nine artifacts. Publish the corrected head and request fresh independent review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:aae220a3128c365f21be2ff473e7514b70683d47","binding":"assigned","head":"77cbe18c940b28476a3399e62aa4abe8a32e3ffd","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:40182d0dfaf44e2bebca67eae329841a5fbd5172\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c9a4d5c6407568fe4c75854268e844718cbec6dd\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c134b3608d809da0a639bf09bf771f967c138d1f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}